# Motion-Informed Keypoint Pruning for Efficient LightGlue Feature Matchign

## Setup

From the project root, activate your vritual environment and install the dependencies using:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Ensure LightGlue is installed and the TUM RGB-D Freiburg1 XYZ dataset is extracted in the project root. The dataset should already be given as part of this project GitHub but can be alternatively found at the following link: https://cvg.cit.tum.de/data/datasets/rgbd-dataset/download

## Running the demo 

```bash
python demo/demo.py
```

Visualizes the motion-informed keypoint pruning and the resulting LightGlue matches

## Running the Experiments

As part of this project three experiments were ran. More information on specifs can be found in the experiments folder README.

Or the following command can be ran to have a basic experiment:
```bash
python results/experiment_1_speed.py --motion random --gaps 10 50 100 200 --pairs-per-gap 5 --repeats 2 --out experiment1/results/random
```

All commands should be ran from the project root. Generated visualization, statistics and plots are saved in the `results/` folder.